---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Kessik: Claude Code on your Mac, from your iPhone">
  <section>
    <h1>Claude Code on your Mac, from your iPhone.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Kessik opens Claude Code on your Mac over SSH. Every session starts inside tmux, so it keeps
      running when your phone locks, loses signal or closes the terminal. Attach to the same session
      later and carry on.
    </p>
    <div class="badges">
      <a class="button" href="https://apps.apple.com/app/kessik/id6823446723">Download on the App Store</a>
      <a class="button ghost" href="/support">Get help</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Sessions that stay alive</h3>
      <p>New Claude sessions start in tmux. Picking the same folder again attaches to the session that already exists.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>A real terminal</h3>
      <p>A key bar adds esc, ctrl, tab, arrows and shell symbols. Swipe to scroll history. Pinch to resize text.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Buttons for prompts</h3>
      <p>When Claude Code shows a numbered menu, such as a permission prompt, Kessik shows one button for each option.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Photos and ports</h3>
      <p>Send a photo to the Mac for a Claude prompt. Preview a dev server port from your Mac in Safari inside the app.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Keys stay on the phone</h3>
      <p>Use an ed25519 key made in the app or a password. Both are kept in the iPhone Keychain. Host key changes stop the connection.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Reach it anywhere</h3>
      <p>Find Macs on your Wi-Fi with Bonjour, or switch to the Tailscale address to connect on any network.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What you need on the Mac</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Remote Login turned on in System Settings, General, Sharing.</li>
      <li>tmux, installed with <code>brew install tmux</code>.</li>
      <li>Claude Code, signed in once by running <code>claude</code> in Terminal.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Kessik needs an iPhone with iOS 17 or later. Tailscale is optional. Four guides in the app cover each step.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>No server, no tracking</h2>
    <p>
      Kessik has no server of its own and collects no data. It connects only to the Mac you choose.
      Read the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
